            <ArticleTitle>Primary torsion of the greater omentum: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>691-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of primary omental torsion that occurred in a 21-year-old man who presented with right lower quadrant abdominal pain. His provisional diagnosis was appendicitis. He was explored for appendicitis but the finding was twisted omentum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
